# Go services

- Pass `context.Context` as the first argument on all blocking and I/O functions.
- Wrap errors with `%w` and a short op name: `fmt.Errorf("store.insertPlacement: %w", err)`.
- Never `panic` in `cmd/agent` (providers run this). `log.Fatal` only in `main` on irrecoverable startup failure.
- Structured logs: `log/slog`. Never log plaintext, keys, wrapped keys, passphrases, or raw ticket secrets.
- HTTP: `GET /healthz` on every long-running process. Timeouts on clients and servers.
- Tests are table-driven. Prefer `t.Parallel()` for pure functions.

```go
// BAD
func Place(n Node) { panic("no capacity") }

// GOOD
func Place(ctx context.Context, n Node) error {
    if n.FreeBytes < 1 {
        return fmt.Errorf("scheduler.place: node %s has no capacity", n.ID)
    }
    return nil
}
```
